{
  "slug": "ponytail",
  "name": "Ponytail",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Lazy senior dev mode. Forces the simplest, shortest solution that actually works: YAGNI, stdlib first, no unrequested abstractions.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **6 skills**, **6 commands**, a **3-trigger hook set** and an MCP server, all built on one YAGNI decision ladder the agent climbs before it writes code.\n\n- **Skills**: `ponytail` (the ladder, at `lite`, `full` or `ultra` intensity), `ponytail-review` (diff review that hunts over-engineering only), `ponytail-audit`, `ponytail-debt`, `ponytail-gain`, `ponytail-help`\n- **Hooks**: `SessionStart`, `SubagentStart` and `UserPromptSubmit` inject the ruleset and track the active mode — the configuration the published benchmarks measure\n- **Also ships**: a `ponytail-mcp` server and rule files for Cursor, Windsurf, Cline, Qoder, Codex, OpenCode and Copilot",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot",
    "antigravity",
    "opencode",
    "codex"
  ],
  "pluginType": "wrapper",
  "wrapper": "skill",
  "sourceType": "community",
